 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Hardware Requirements**: Requires LPV (Light Propagation Volumes) and `GL_ARB_shader_image_load_store` support. Gracefully degrades to SSRT if these are not met [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision Issues**: Division-by-zero or NaN sources in TAA resolve pass (e.g., `invTonemap()`) can produce black pixel artifacts, especially on hardware with aggressive FP16 FTZ behaviour (e.g., NVIDIA RTX 5000 series). Epsilon guards are required to prevent division by zero [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Self-Intersection**: Ray bias must be included in DDA traversal to avoid self-intersection and handle near-parallel rays gracefully [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Visual Mismatch**: Reflection fallback must scale voxel lighting to match typical sky-reflection brightness ranges to avoid visual mismatch [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Hardware Support:** Requires LPV and `GL_ARB_shader_image_load_store` support. Gracefully degrades to SSRT if these are not met [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Precision Artifacts:** Division-by-zero or NaN sources in related passes (e.g., TAA resolve) can produce black pixel artifacts, especially on hardware with aggressive FP16 FTZ behavior (e.g., NVIDIA RTX 5000 series) [S1, unofficial]. Epsilon guards are required in tonemapping and blending calculations [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Self-Intersection:** Near-parallel rays or origins inside voxels require ray bias to prevent immediate re-intersection [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: Not given in the sources [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: Not given in the sources [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance**: Depends on grid resolution (128³) and step limits. The method is efficient as it avoids complex scene traversal, relying on the uniform grid structure [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths**: Provides scene-wide GI and reflections independent of camera position or screen-space coverage. Drop-in replacement for SSRT [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations**: Requires LPV and specific OpenGL extensions. Lower resolution than path tracing. Artifacts may occur if LPV data is not properly propagated [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use**: When screen-space methods (SSRT/SSR) fail due to occlusion or incomplete coverage, and LPV is available [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When Not to Use**: When hardware does not support required extensions or LPV is not enabled [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of steps in the DDA traversal. For GI, complexity is $O(S \cdot N)$ where $S$ is `VOXEL_GI_SAMPLES` (default 4) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V)$ for the voxel grid, where $V = 128^3$ blocks [S1, unofficial]. No additional buffers are needed beyond the existing LPV and mask textures [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Provides global illumination and reflections in scenes where screen-space methods fail (e.g., off-screen objects, low coverage) [S1, unofficial]. Drop-in replacement for SSRT [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Limitations:** Relies on the quality of the LPV propagation. Blocky artifacts may appear at low resolutions. Requires specific hardware features (`GL_ARB_shader_image_load_store`) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **When to Use:** When screen-space GI/Reflections are insufficient or unavailable, and LPV is already in use.
+*   **When Not to Use:** On hardware lacking required GL extensions, or when high-fidelity, smooth reflections are required without the blocky nature of voxel data.
 
 ## Background
-The method was implemented by nyzxor as a pull request to the Eclipse-Shader (an edit of Chocapic13 V9 / Bliss) for Minecraft, integrated via Iris [S1, unofficial]. It was merged into the Unstable branch on May 22, 2026 [S1, unofficial]. The implementation builds on the principles of 3D-DDA traversal shared by the Regular Grid Traversal family [4091-voxel-based-ray-tracing-for-gi-and-specular-reflections, 4240-optimised-voxel-ray-marching] and links to [Regular Grid Traversal](5939-regular-grid-traversal.md) [S1, unofficial].
+This method was implemented by nyzxor as a pull request to the Eclipse-Shader (an edit of Chocapic13 V9 / Bliss) for Minecraft, integrated via the Iris shader mod [S1, unofficial]. It was added to provide an alternative global illumination method and a fallback for specular reflections [S1, unofficial]. The implementation utilizes the existing 128³ block-occupancy voxel grid (`imgVoxelMask`) populated in the shadow pass, requiring no new buffers or passes [S1, unofficial].
 
